  paragraphs:
    - Thalassaemias are inherited disorders in which the body makes too little of one of haemoglobin's chains. Two carrier parents can have a child with thalassaemia major, who needs lifelong transfusions. Finding carriers early lets couples make informed choices.
    - On average 3 to 4 in 100 Indians carry beta thalassaemia; when both parents are carriers, each pregnancy has a 1 in 4 chance of thalassaemia major.
